  "narrative": {
    "intro": "New Mexico federal contract obligations total $14.6B in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 8,973 awards with an average award size of $1.6M. Obligations are up 7.9% year over year. The Department of Energy is the largest buyer in the state, accounting for $10.6B in obligations. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry by obligations at $10.5B, reflecting the concentration of large site operations and management contracts. TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC and NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC are the largest vendors, with $5.3B and $5.2B in obligations respectively. Yearly totals have trended upward from $11.6B in FY21 to $14.6B in FY26. Contracting activity also includes construction sectors such as Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $2B and Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction at $299M. The distribution of obligations shows a heavy skew toward a few large buyers and vendors, while other agencies and industries account for much smaller shares of the state total.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies drive federal contracting in New Mexico?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy drives federal contracting in New Mexico with $10.6B in obligations. The Department of Homeland Security follows with $2B, and the Department of Defense follows with $974M. Other buying agencies include the Department of the Interior with $409M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $272M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who and which industries capture the largest shares of obligations?",
        "body": "TRIAD NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC and NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC capture the largest vendor shares with $5.3B and $5.2B respectively. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry by obligations at $10.5B, followed by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $2B and Water and Sewer Line and Related Structures Construction at $299M. Several construction and research NAICS categories appear among the top industries, showing a mix of operations, construction, and R&D work."
      }
    ]
  },
